content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-105, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22000, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.9 mm/s is in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation') on the HF-300 severity chart (Figure 3). It is 0.6 mm/s below the Zone C boundary of 4.5 mm/s and well below the Zone D stop limit of 7.1 mm/s. The site immediate-stop rule applies only to the manufacturer's highest zone (Zone D), so it is not triggered. This assumes the reading is RMS velocity on a bearing housing, as the chart requires.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature 71 C is 1 C above the manufacturer's normal limit (up to 70 C). It is below the alarm (80 C) and trip (90 C) limits. Because it is not above the alarm limit, the site rule requiring a priority-1 work order within the shift does not apply. It is still abnormal and needs investigation.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The shaft seal is leaking. The manufacturer's corrective action is to replace the mechanical seal (section 5.2) and check alignment (section 5.4). The seal relies on a Plan 11 flush and must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Priority is set to P2 (planned and scheduled, not an immediate stop). No reading reaches a manufacturer stop or alarm limit or a site P1 trigger. However, the active seal leak and the above-normal bearing temperature mean the work should not wait for routine maintenance.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C15",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces. This is the most likely cause, and it is aggravated if the original component seal HF3-450 is fitted. SB-2026-014 reports early failure of HF3-450 on pumps from serial HF3-22000 because of a revised sleeve tolerance, and this pump is HF3-22000.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is listed as a cause of all three symptoms: seal leakage, raised vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal has run dry, for example through loss of the Plan 11 flush from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing over-greasing or bearing wear, which would explain the temperature just above normal. Bearing wear can also contribute to vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation. These are lower likelihood because vibration is still in Zone B.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before work, obtain a line-break permit. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC. Close and lock the suction and discharge valves (mechanical isolation).",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drain and vent the pump casing. Isolate and drain the pump as step 1 of section 5.2.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Get the lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor. Rig certified lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly. The casing and pipework can stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and the impeller. Inspect the impeller for damage or imbalance as a possible vibration source.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and shaft sleeve. Record which seal was fitted (HF3-450 or HF3-450B) and the condition of the seal faces.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring. Replace the sleeve if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B. Do NOT fit HF3-450. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120. It must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, inspect both bearings and check the grease quantity. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both as a pair (section 5.3).",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and torque to the following values on lightly oiled threads: impeller nut M24 = 160 Nm; seal gland nuts M10 = 30 Nm (SB-2026-014 value for HF3-450B, not the 25 Nm in Table 5); bearing housing bolts M12 = 85 Nm; casing bolts M16 = 210 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out laser shaft alignment (section 5.4) to tolerances of 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular. This is required after work that moves the bearing housing and is also recommended for the seal leak.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is in place and the casing is fully flooded and vented. The seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading on Figure 3. Monitor bearing housing temperatures against the limits: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency: fit only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Contingency: replace as a pair only if inspection shows wear.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Contingency: replace as a pair with HF3-512 only if inspection shows wear.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC; mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Line-break permit; drain and vent the pump before opening.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, which is over the 25 kg limit. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not run the pump dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration ever reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS), stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If bearing temperature exceeds 80 C (alarm), raise a P1 work order within the shift. Neither applies at present.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency: bearing replacement (pair), 6.0 hours, 2 technicians, only if the bearings are found worn.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: the O&M manual parts list gives component seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) says do NOT fit HF3-450 and use cartridge seal HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above. This pump is serial HF3-22000, which is within the 'and above' range, so the bulletin applies and HF3-450B must be fitted.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. The bulletin states Table 5 continues to apply only below serial HF3-22000. This pump is HF3-22000, so 30 Nm applies. All other Table 5 torques (impeller nut 160 Nm, casing bolts 210 Nm, bearing housing bolts 85 Nm) are not changed by the bulletin and still apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve handling: manual section 5.2 says only to inspect the sleeve for scoring, with no acceptance limit. SB-2026-014 adds a replacement criterion (scoring deeper than 0.1 mm) and says no sleeve measurement is needed with pre-set HF3-450B. The bulletin's criteria apply to this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the 3.9 mm/s reading an RMS velocity taken on a bearing housing, and is it the highest of the drive-end and non-drive-end readings? Figure 3 classification assumes RMS on the bearing housings.",
    "The non-drive-end bearing housing temperature and the temperature trend were not reported. Is 71 C stable or rising?",
    "Which seal is currently fitted (HF3-450 or HF3-450B)? The evidence does not say, so the link to the SB early-failure mode cannot be confirmed until it is removed.",
    "Leak rate and severity were not reported. If the leak is heavy or the flush is lost, risk of running dry may justify an earlier stop; the evidence gives no leak-rate limit.",
    "Is the filtered-water line chemically dosed? If so, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are also required under SSP-07.",
    "The evidence gives no grease quantity or regreasing interval, so over-greasing cannot be assessed against a specification.",
    "The evidence gives no torque for coupling or motor hold-down fasteners, if these are disturbed during alignment.",
    "Stock and lead time for HF3-450B are not known."
  ]
}
